{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-124",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "Following inverse-theorem complete self-proof request: two planes alpha and beta perpendicular to m, cut by auxiliary intersecting planes gamma1 and gamma2. A and B lie on m; a1/a2 and b1/b2 are the four respective section lines. No proof conclusion or answer is added. True spatial intersections and perpendicularity are checked by fig-124.geometry.mjs; their screen projections are not required to be perpendicular.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/9-10g/figures/fig-124.png",
      "sha256": "a2be1eed7ff78376e2ab6c65fbd6a81fdde85fc52034cc0096c5b1ab05a3b387"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "geo910-c1-s3-n33",
        "text": "**定理19. 垂直于两个平行平面中一个的直线必垂直于另一个.**"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "geo910-c1-s3-n33",
        "text": "证明. 设$a\\cap\\alpha=M$，$a\\cap\\beta=N$(图123). 向量$\\overrightarrow{MN}$将直线$a$映射成自身，而将平面$\\alpha$映射成平面$\\beta$(§17). 在位移下保持直线和平面的垂直性(§28)，因而$a\\perp\\beta$. $\\blacksquare$"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "geo910-c1-s3-n33",
        "text": "逆命题也成立：同垂直于同一条直线的两个平面平行. 自己证明这个定理(图124)."
      }
    ],
