        "description": "Pixels show two upright four-sided auxiliary planes labelled gamma1 on the left and gamma2 on the right. They share the central vertical line m. Their top vertices meet above A; their bottom edges meet at the filled dot B. The upper filled dot A is on that same central line. Line m is solid down to A, dashed from A through the front portion of alpha, then solid down to B. It does not continue below B. The outside upright boundaries and top boundaries are solid. No arrows, perpendicular-square marks, angle arcs, equal-length ticks or numeric labels appear; the small heavy join at the right beta rear-edge crossing is a stroke join, not an arrowhead. Modern additions: faint plane fills and regularized bounds only.",
