        "id": "source-four-section-lines",
        "description": "Pixels label a2 on the upper-left segment from A to the left outer upright boundary, a1 on the upper-right segment from A to the right upright boundary, b2 on the lower-left segment from B to the left upright boundary, and b1 on the lower-right segment from B to the right upright boundary. Thus a1 and a2 meet at A, b1 and b2 at B; each corresponding pair belongs to the same auxiliary plane. Source endpoints on the outer bounds are unlabelled and unmarked, not extra named points. All four section segments are solid. The inverse theorem asks for a complete self-proof, and exercise305 has no figure reference.",
